;; scatter (FEAT-018 S-B) — fan-out: spawn one await-free child per item.
;;
;; `spawn-session` lifted over a collection. Each item's child gets a prompt built
;; by concatenating the shared `prompt` prefix with the item (so the shared prefix
;; is identical across the burst — cache-friendly, the "smart passing"). Returns
;; the list of mission handles; the caller awaits them with `gather`.
;;
;; All children join the SAME region (a fresh Fork-A region when :region is absent
;; would isolate each child — so scatter REQUIRES a shared :region to fan into,
;; defaulting children to coordinate on one blackboard). The cohort posts findings
;; there; the parent folds them.
;;
;; Args (data/*):
;;   items           — the collection to fan out over (required, a list).
;;   prompt          — the shared prompt prefix; each child gets (str prompt item).
;;   region          — the shared region all children coordinate in (required for
;;                     a meaningful fan-out+fold; absent -> each child isolated).
;;   tools           — optional capability subset for every child.
;;   inherit-memory  — optional def-env slice seeded into every child (uniform ->
;;                     cache-neutral).
;;
;; Returns [handle ...] — one mission handle per item, in order.
(map (fn [item]
       (tool/spawn-session {:prompt (str data/prompt item)
                            :region data/region
                            :tools data/tools
                            :inherit-memory data/inherit-memory}))
     data/items)
